nd-async-load-crash-FIXED.md) â€” **DONE 2026-07-02, committed+pushed, verified 
(`master`=`b9c890992`).** Two independent bugs, each root-caused via a 4-consultant crew round. 
**(1) gl11 chase-camera saw THROUGH interior walls** (`a976f81e2`, CONSULT-54): camera/collision 
code is byte-identical to SWG-Source â€” the real bug is gl11-mechanical: 
`Direct3d11_StaticVertexBufferData::lock(readOnly)` returned all-ZEROS (DEFAULT bufs can't be 
GPU-read-back), so `collisionSplit()` built every mesh's collision triangles from zeroed vertices 
â†’ walls collapsed to origin â†’ `collide()` never hit them. FIX = **CPU shadow on the static VB** 
(mirror the cape-spike IB-shadow fix); restores ALL gl11 mesh-collision-from-VB. Then **removed the 
interior zoom-cap band-aid** (`freeChaseCameraInteriorMaximumZoom`); door-snap fixes untouched. 
Residual accepted: fast-rotation fraction-of-a-second peek = our `cs_cameraPullInSpeed` rate-limit 
(Opus's penetration-bound/persistence-gate fix on file if we tighten). **(2) intermittent "Unknown 
shader template tag" async-load crash** (`9c03f53c5`, CONSULT-55, "frequent after rebuild"): 
`TreeFile::SearchCache::m_cachedFileMap` (std::map) read by the async-loader thread while the main 
thread inserts across zone-in frames â€” **NO lock** â†’ concurrent find/insert UB â†’ garbage IFF 
tag; `ZlibFile::decompress` swallowing `expand()`'s failure amplified it. FIX = **leaf mutex on the 
SearchCache map** (I/O stays outside; deadlock-free) + **fail-loud `ZlibFile::decompress`**. 
Verified across several post-rebuild launches. Cleanup `b9c890992` (redundant stage/override 
band-aids + validateIff diagnostic removed). Memories: 
`project_d3d11_static_vb_readback_zero_collision`, 
`project_treefile_searchcache_unlocked_map_async_crash`.
